WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.910
- Speaking of walking, I heard
that you asked your father

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.390
on "Young Rock," the character,
to take a walk with you.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.800
- Yes.
- You wanted to do that

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.910
with your dad and you didn't get it

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.411
and so is that what happened?

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.244
- So, yes.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.650
So this is Joseph Lee Anderson

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.770
and he's the man who plays
my dad on "Young Rock."

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.470
And my dad was a professional wrestler,

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.660
bad dude in the game,

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.100
one of the first black champions

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.750
in the world of pro wrestling.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.430
And my dad passed away
suddenly two years ago,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.160
and I never had a chance
to say goodbye to him.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.320
And when somebody (snaps) goes like that,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.030
and plus we had a
complicated relationship,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.660
so when he died, I was
like, man, there's just,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.920
we had more talking to do.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.910
We had more stuff

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.500
to take care of,
- Yeah.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.450
- unanswered questions, man.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.510
And so I still reconcile
with that still today and-

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.437
- Yeah.
- but yet this surreal show,

00:00:50.437 --> 00:00:53.310
"Young Rock," has been shooting
for almost three years.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.100
I've never met any of the
actors because of Covid.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.360
So we
- What?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.800
Yeah, dude.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.506
We just shot in Memphis three weeks ago.

00:01:01.506 --> 00:01:02.339
- Yeah.
I shot all my stuff,

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:03.810
and the cast flew over

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.660
and I finally got a chance
to meet all the cast,

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.520
and this guy, Joseph Lee Anderson,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.890
who plays my dad, and he,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.220
if you ever see a picture
of my dad, it's so striking.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.350
And I hugged this guy
and it was so emotional,

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.250
I didn't want to let him go,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.270
'cause it's like hugging your,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.103
- Aw.

00:01:19.103 --> 00:01:19.980
- the one who you lost.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.440
And so I've never took a walk with my dad,

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.170
because he's like, my dad was like,

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.070
he's like a dude who
was stunted emotionally.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.223
- A dude bro. That's what we called 'em.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.056
- A dude bro.
- Yeah.

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:31.889
- He was like a dude bro.

00:01:31.889 --> 00:01:33.300
- We called them dude bros. (laughs)

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.133
- So we never had these moments,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.127
so, I told him, I said,

00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:38.280
"Hey man, would you mind
taking a walk with me?"

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.660
He's like, "Yeah, let's just take a walk."

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.270
So I took a walk. It was
like walking with my old man.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.027
That's so cool.
- It was really special. Yeah.

00:01:45.027 --> 00:01:45.860
(audience applauds)
- I'm sorry that you

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.190
didn't get, I never got
that either, with my father.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.180
He passed away.
- Oh really?

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.830
Yeah. But sometimes it's hard.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.360
Sometimes you try and it doesn't work.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.400
And then sometimes I do
feel like people come

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.550
into your lives to kind of
represent maybe what was missing.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.553
- Yes.

00:01:57.553 --> 00:01:59.130
- And then you have to be open to that.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:01:59.963
- Yes.
- I feel like,

00:01:59.963 --> 00:02:01.794
I mean, that's how my therapy sessions go.

00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:02.627
(both laugh)

00:02:02.627 --> 00:02:03.460
- Yes. No, no, no.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.293
You're right.

00:02:04.293 --> 00:02:05.126
- That's my life.

00:02:05.126 --> 00:02:06.090
- Also, what I feel like is,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.220
what's interesting is,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.930
we had a complicated relationship,

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.683
but now that he's gone,
I feel like we're closer.

00:02:15.102 --> 00:02:15.935
- Yeah.
- In this crazy way,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.820
where I could just talk
to him at any point.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.980
And also what I realized is,

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.517
I find myself more and more
thinking about the good stuff.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.400
- Yeah.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.500
- And not the stuff that
was kind of funky, you know?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.653
- Yeah.
(audience applauds)

